#  Linux Directory Structure

| Directory | Purpose | Why It Matters to a SOC Analyst |
|-----------|---------|---------------------------------|
| `/` | Root directory | Starting point of the Linux file system. |
| `/home` | User home directories | Useful when investigating user activity and stored files. |
| `/root` | Root user's home directory | Contains files owned by the administrator account. |
| `/etc` | System configuration files | Critical when reviewing system settings and service configurations. |
| `/var` | Variable data and logs | Contains system and application logs used during investigations. |
| `/tmp` | Temporary files | Frequently abused by malware to store temporary payloads. |
| `/usr` | Installed applications | Helps verify installed software and binaries. |
| `/bin` | Essential system binaries | Stores core Linux commands required for system operation. |
| `/opt` | Optional software | Often contains third-party applications. |

