# Understanding Linux File Permissions

Example:

```text
-rwxr-xr--
```

### Breakdown

| Component | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| `-` | Regular file |
| `rwx` | Owner has Read, Write, and Execute permissions |
| `r-x` | Group has Read and Execute permissions |
| `r--` | Others have Read-only permission |

### Key Learning

The owner has full control of the file, members of the assigned group can read and execute it, while everyone else can only read it.

Linux permissions follow the **Principle of Least Privilege**, ensuring users only receive the minimum access required to perform their tasks.

